<header><p class="st-kicker">other · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Federal League</h1><p class="st-meta">1814 CE – 1820 CE · capital Purificación</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A league of provinces led by José Artigas that challenged Buenos Aires with a vision of federal democracy in the River Plate region.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1814 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Gervasio Artigas</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eastern-province">Eastern Province</a>, drew the provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entre-rios-province">Entre Ríos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corrientes">Corrientes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-fe-argentina">Santa Fe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/misiones-province">Misiones</a>, and briefly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, into an alliance against the centralism of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>. Artigas took the title Protector of the Free Peoples. In 1815 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-oriente">Congress of Oriente</a> met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concepcion-del-uruguay">Concepción del Uruguay</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league was a loose alliance of provincial caudillos rather than a state. It defended provincial autonomy, free trade on the rivers and the rights of rural people. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">Artigas</a> directed it from his camp at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purificacion-uruguay">Purificación</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paysandu">Paysandú</a> on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/oriental-republic-of-uruguay">Uruguay</a> river. Indigenous Guaraní of the missions, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-guazurary">Andrés Guazurary</a>, fought with him.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Portugal's invasion of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eastern-province">Banda Oriental</a> from 1816 drained the league. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">Artigas</a>'s defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tacuarembo">Tacuarembó</a> in 1820, his allies <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Francisco Ramírez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-lopez">Estanislao López</a> made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pilar">Treaty of Pilar</a>. Artigas went into exile in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-paraguay">Paraguay</a>, where he died in 1850.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/federal-league.jpg" alt="Federal League" width="320" height="402"><figcaption>Image: Photograph by Moffett Studio, Chicago Restoration by Animalparty · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_A._Gilmore,_President,_Federal_League_(baseball)_-_retouched.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1814 CE – 1820 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Purificación</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>José Gervasio Artigas, Francisco Ramírez, Estanislao López</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uruguay">Uruguay</a>, <a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>League of the Free Peoples, Liga Federal, Liga de los Pueblos Libres</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=federal-league" aria-label="Federal League on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3246 3375 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Federal League lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3517 3686h0M3505 3614h0M3575 3696h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3566 3631h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M3566 3631h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Uruguay. <a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=federal-league">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
